<title>POLAND: Polish winter rapeseed, barley damaged by weather.</title>
<headline>Polish winter rapeseed, barley damaged by weather.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-02-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Poland's winter rapeseed and barley crops were severely hit by cold weather with little snow cover to protect plants, an official from the Institute of Meteorology and Water Management (IMGW) said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;There is significant damage in winter rapeseed and barley crops as the cold easily penetrated the ground with little snow for protection,&quot; IMGW specialist Anna Strzelczak told Reuters.</p>
<p>She said roughly 20 to 40 percent of winter rape and barley had been damaged over the winter and between one and 20 percent of winter wheat and rye sustained damage.</p>
<p>Just 61 percent of the rapeseed crop survived the harsh 1995/96 winter, while 81 percent of barley, 89 percent of wheat and 90 of rye successfully sprouted last spring.</p>
<p>--Wojciech Moskwa, Warsaw newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
